│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parameter_sharing_entangling_layers                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach has several limitations:                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter Economy**: The seed uses 24 distinct parameters (RY and RZ on all 8        │
│                          │ qubits, pre and post), which is inefficient. With only ~32 training samples and high      │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.31), we need dramatically fewer parameters.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Poor Generalization**: The model overfits (train acc 0.88, test acc 0.56),           │
│                          │ suggesting it memorizes the small training set rather than learning generalizable         │
│                          │ features. The worst-group margin is only 0.03, indicating the classifier fails on hard    │
│                          │ samples.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Weak Entanglement**: The architecture uses only a simple line of CZ gates, lacking   │
│                          │ rich qubit correlations needed for complex state classification.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Parameter Sharing Underutilized**: The block is repeated 3 times with identical      │
│                          │ parameters. We can use this repetition more strategically.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 5. **High Train-Test Gap**: Indicates insufficient regularization through structure.      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **New approach:**                                                                         │
│                          │ - **Aggressive parameter sharing**: Use only 4-6 distinct parameters per block by sharing │
│                          │ angles across qubits with symmetry                                                        │
│                          │ - **Dense all-to-all entanglement**: Replace linear CZ chain with a 2-layer all-to-all    │
│                          │ connectivity pattern using parametrized two-qubit gates (XX, YY, ZZ) to create richer     │
│                          │ correlations                                                                              │
│                          │ - **Minimal single-qubit rotations**: Only 2 shared RY parameters that apply to disjoint  │
│                          │ qubit pairs                                                                               │
│                          │ - **Parametrized entanglement**: Use XX/YY Ising couplings (fewer distinct angles needed) │
│                          │ rather than fixed CZ gates                                                                │
│                          │ - **Alternating block structure**: Rotate between different parameter groups across       │
│                          │ repetitions to avoid overfitting while maintaining count                                  │
│                          │ - This reduces effective parameters from 26 to ~12-16, forcing the model to learn more    │
│                          │ generalizable representations                                                             │
