│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a score of 0.54 with 12 distinct parameters and strong       │
│                          │ validation accuracy (0.96). However, the worst_group_margin_mean (0.31) indicates that    │
│                          │ edge-case correlations remain underexploited, limiting robustness on hard samples.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation to add a targeted IsingZZ cross-coupling, I add a single ZZ  │
│                          │ gate between qubits (3, 4) under a new parameter "zz_bridge". This complements the        │
│                          │ existing near-neighbor and long-range structure:                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Current structure: RY (2 shared params) + XX neighbors (4 params) + RZ (2 shared        │
│                          │ params) + YY staggered (3 params) + ZZ diagonal (1 shared param) = 12 params              │
│                          │ - New structure: same as above + 1 new ZZ gate = 13 params                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The (3,4) bridge connects the middle of the qubit chain and lies between established      │
│                          │ long-range diagonal couplings (0,3) and (4,7). This strategic placement learns additional │
│                          │ non-stoquastic correlations that should specifically improve margins on the               │
│                          │ worst-performing hidden groups without incurring significant parameter cost or            │
│                          │ overfitting penalty, since the gain comes from generalization robustness rather than      │
│                          │ memorization.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The net effect: +1 parameter, but improved worst-group margins and likely better test     │
│                          │ accuracy through enhanced separation of difficult samples.                                │
