│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_depth_add_yy_link                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests reducing N_REPEATS from 3 to 2 and adding a targeted second   │
│                          │ cross-YY link to maintain expressivity while reducing circuit depth and the               │
│                          │ generalization gap.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Current metrics show:                                                                     │
│                          │ - depth_mean: 15.00 (per block × 3 repeats = ~45 total depth)                             │
│                          │ - generalization_gap_mean: 0.10 (already good but can improve)                            │
│                          │ - worst_group_margin_mean: 0.31 (hardest samples need better separation)                  │
│                          │ - n_distinct_params: 12 (room to stay lean)                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Reduce N_REPEATS to 2: This cuts total circuit depth from ~45 to ~30, reducing         │
│                          │ overfitting and improving trainability on few samples. The depth was identified as a      │
│                          │ sweet spot around 8-12 per block in prior analysis.                                       │
│                          │ 2. Add a second targeted YY gate between qubits (1, 3) under a new shared key "cross_b":  │
│                          │ This adds one more expressivity channel without fragmenting parameter count. YY gates     │
│                          │ have shown strong performance for capturing non-trivial correlations.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected impact:                                                                          │
│                          │ - Reduce total depth by ~33%, improving generalization on held-out samples                │
│                          │ - Maintain or improve worst-group margin by introducing targeted cross-coupling that      │
│                          │ complements the existing staggered YY links                                               │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count reasonable by adding one new distinct parameter                    │
│                          │ - Converge faster due to simpler landscape                                                │
│                          │ - Improve parameter efficiency and reduce the train-test gap                              │
