                         Patch Metadata - Gen 15/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_sparse_xx_star_layer                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.49 combined score with 11 distinct parameters. Analysis of │
│                          │ the prior generations shows:                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Gen 1** (score 0.51): 7 distinct params, simpler structure with shared RY/RZ and     │
│                          │ diagonal ZZ links                                                                         │
│                          │ 2. **Gen 2** (score 0.54, best): 12 distinct params, achieved higher accuracy (0.96       │
│                          │ validation, 0.90 test) and better worst-group margin (0.31) with more diverse             │
│                          │ entanglement                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program (0.49) has regressed: its worst-group margin dropped to 0.22,         │
│                          │ indicating failure on hard samples. It has fewer parameters (11) than Gen 2 but worse     │
│                          │ performance, suggesting the current architecture lacks sufficient non-local entanglement  │
│                          │ diversity.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key insight**: Gen 2's superior performance on hard samples came from mixed-channel     │
│                          │ entanglement (XX, YY, ZZ on different qubit pairs). The current program only uses XX      │
│                          │ (nearest-neighbor pairs) and limited diagonal ZZ, missing global correlations.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed fix**: Append a sparse "star" IsingXX layer connecting hub qubit 0 to          │
│                          │ peripheral qubits 2, 4, 6 using a single shared parameter "xx_star". This:                │
│                          │ - Adds **+1 distinct parameter** (minimal cost, maximizes parameter economy)              │
│                          │ - Creates **+3 non-local XX gates** capturing long-range correlations                     │
│                          │ - Complements existing nearest-neighbor XX (which saturates local structure)              │
│                          │ - Mirrors Gen 2's diversity strategy but with tighter parameter sharing                   │
│                          │ - Expected improvement: better separation on hard (grouped) validation samples via global │
│                          │ entanglement                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Cost: 11 → 12 distinct parameters (+1), gate_count 72 → 75 (+3). This matches Gen 2's     │
│                          │ parameter count but with a more targeted sparse structure.                                │
