│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_sparse_star_xx_layer                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.51) has a dense, high-gate-count structure (96 gates) that   │
│                          │ may be overfitting despite aggressive parameter sharing (only 7 distinct parameters). The │
│                          │ prior program (score 0.54) achieved better validation accuracy (0.96 vs 0.89), validation │
│                          │ margin (0.58 vs 0.57), and worst-group margin (0.31 vs 0.36), with slightly more distinct │
│                          │ parameters (12 vs 7) but better generalization.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation to add a sparse "star" IsingXX layer is well-motivated:                │
│                          │ 1. **Non-local entanglement**: The current dense structure has local/mid-range XX and YY  │
│                          │ gates but lacks global long-range coupling. A star pattern (hub qubit 0 connected to      │
│                          │ qubits 2, 4, 6) introduces orthogonal entanglement channels.                              │
│                          │ 2. **Parameter efficiency**: Uses only +1 new parameter name ("xx_star") shared across 3  │
│                          │ gates, maintaining strong parameter economy while adding expressiveness.                  │
│                          │ 3. **Generalization**: Sparse architectures with strategic long-range links generalize    │
│                          │ better from few examples than dense all-to-all patterns.                                  │
│                          │ 4. **Gate economy**: Adds only +3 gates, keeping depth/gate count reasonable.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The edit removes the overly dense YY layer (8 gates, 2 params) and replaces some          │
│                          │ redundancy in the current structure with a focused sparse entangling layer. This should:  │
│                          │ - Reduce train-test gap by avoiding dense fitting                                         │
│                          │ - Improve worst-group margin by capturing global correlations                             │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count low for better efficiency                                          │
