│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_sparse_crz_cross_layer                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.45) has degraded from the second prior program (score 0.54), │
│                          │ which achieved better worst_group_margin (0.31 vs 0.18) and validation accuracy (0.96 vs  │
│                          │ 0.84). The key difference is that the current program uses 8 distinct parameters with a   │
│                          │ simpler, less expressive structure.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second program achieved success by mixing multiple entanglement types (XX, YY, ZZ)    │
│                          │ with dense connectivity patterns and parameter sharing. The recommendation to add sparse  │
│                          │ CRZ gates after YY entanglement aligns well with this insight: CRZ (controlled-phase      │
│                          │ rotation) injected at the right connectivity can mix long-range phase correlations        │
│                          │ without significantly increasing parameter count.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Add a new `_build_crz_cross_layer()` that introduces two CRZ gates on pairs (1, 3) and │
│                          │ (5, 7), both sharing a new parameter "crz_cross". This is minimal (+2 gates, +1           │
│                          │ parameter) and targets the spatial structure between the YY cross-layer coupling (qubits  │
│                          │ 1,3 and 4,6) and long-range ZZ layer.                                                     │
│                          │ 2. Insert this layer after the cross_layer_coupling to build up phase entanglement on     │
│                          │ diagonals where the previous YY gates activated, creating richer correlations without     │
│                          │ depth explosion.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. This design mirrors the second program's success: it uses parameter sharing to keep    │
│                          │ the count low while injecting controlled multi-qubit effects at strategic points.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Richer phase-based entanglement between already-coupled qubits should boost             │
│                          │ worst_group_margin by preventing collapse on hard samples                                 │
│                          │ - Adding one dedicated parameter keeps parameter_efficiency reasonable                    │
│                          │ - The sparse placement avoids over-complication while enhancing expressivity at           │
│                          │ data-dependent bottlenecks                                                                │
