│ patch_name               │ enhanced_diagonal_entanglement                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has poor worst_group_margin (0.25 vs 0.36 in seed, 0.31 in Gen 3),    │
│                          │ indicating weak separation on hard validation samples. The issue is likely that the       │
│                          │ diagonal ZZ entanglement layer is too sparse (only 2 pairs: (0,4) and (2,6)).             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Proposed fix:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Expand the ZZ layer to include additional diagonal and cross-diagonal pairs while      │
│                          │ maintaining parameter sharing                                                             │
│                          │ 2. Add complementary ZZ pairs on (1,5), (3,7), and (1,6), (3,4) to create more thorough   │
│                          │ long-range connectivity                                                                   │
│                          │ 3. Keep all ZZ gates sharing the same "diag" parameter to avoid parameter explosion       │
│                          │ (stays at 7 distinct params)                                                              │
│                          │ 4. This improves entanglement without increasing parameter count, addressing the          │
│                          │ generalization gap and hard-sample margin                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The expanded diagonal coverage should enable the circuit to separate difficult samples    │
│                          │ better, analogous to how Gen 3's richer structure improved margin from 0.36→0.31          │
│                          │ (actually both are margins; Gen 3's 0.31 vs current's 0.25 means Gen 3 had better         │
│                          │ separation on hard groups).                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Wait, I need to re-read the metrics: worst_group_margin_mean is what we want to maximize. │
│                          │ Gen 3 had 0.31, current has 0.25 - so Gen 3 was better. Higher worst_group_margin is      │
│                          │ better for robustness. Current is worse. Adding more ZZ connections with shared           │
│                          │ parameters should improve this.                                                           │
