│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_balanced_entanglement                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from three candidates:                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the best performer (score 0.54, 12 distinct params)**: The structured approach  │
│                          │ with even/odd parameter sharing on RY/RZ layers, which achieves 96% validation accuracy   │
│                          │ and balanced generalization.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the seed program (score 0.51, 7 distinct params)**: The highly economical       │
│                          │ parameter sharing strategy (ry_even/ry_odd, xx_near/xx_mid, yy_far/yy_diag, rz_final)     │
│                          │ that achieves excellent parameter efficiency (0.09) and worst-group margin (0.36).        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From the current program (score 0.40, 12 distinct params)**: We avoid its sparse     │
│                          │ star-topology entanglement which appears to hurt generalization.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key improvements in the hybrid:**                                                       │
│                          │ - Start with the seed's proven 7-parameter structure (ry_even, ry_odd, xx_near, xx_mid,   │
│                          │ yy_far, yy_diag, rz_final)                                                                │
│                          │ - This minimalist approach with heavy parameter sharing reduces overfitting risk          │
│                          │ - Maintains nearest-neighbor XX gates (proven stable), mid-distance XX gates (cross-layer │
│                          │ correlation), and diagonal YY gates (orthogonal feature extraction)                       │
│                          │ - Removes the problematic non-local XX star topology and excessive per-pair parameters    │
│                          │ - The depth-18 structure with 96 gates provides sufficient expressiveness without         │
│                          │ overparameterization                                                                      │
│                          │ - Expected to score between 0.51-0.54 by balancing parameter economy with validation      │
│                          │ accuracy                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The seed architecture's 0.85 test accuracy, 0.57 validation margin, and 0.36 worst-group  │
│                          │ margin demonstrate robust separation even on hard samples, which is the primary scoring   │
│                          │ criterion.                                                                                │
