                         Patch Metadata - Gen 25/80 - Novelty: 2/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ yy_ring_entanglement_loop                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves 0.46 combined score but trails the second prior program      │
│                          │ (0.54) on worst_group_margin (0.25 vs 0.31). The key observation is:                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Worst-group margin dominance**: The scoring function prioritizes separation of the   │
│                          │ *hardest* validation samples (worst_group_margin is the largest score term). The current  │
│                          │ circuit achieves only 0.25 vs. the prior 0.31, suggesting it lacks sufficient             │
│                          │ entanglement diversity to capture hidden structure in difficult samples.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Parameter economy wins**: The second prior (0.54 score) uses 12 distinct parameters  │
│                          │ across 14 total, achieving better generalization than the current simpler 7-parameter     │
│                          │ design. Yet we want to keep the parameter count reasonable.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Entanglement structure gap**: The current circuit has:                               │
│                          │    - RY (even/odd parity): 2 params                                                       │
│                          │    - XX near-neighbor: 1 param (shared)                                                   │
│                          │    - YY cross-layer: 1 param (shared)                                                     │
│                          │    - ZZ diagonal: 1 param (shared)                                                        │
│                          │    - RZ (even/odd parity): 2 param                                                        │
│                          │    Total: 7 distinct params, but all two-qubit gates share parameters globally, limiting  │
│                          │ expressiveness.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Ring topology insight**: A four-qubit ring of YY gates connecting                    │
│                          │ (0,2)→(2,4)→(4,6)→(6,0) under a *single* new parameter creates:                           │
│                          │    - Non-local entanglement reminiscent of a small MPS "ring" structure                   │
│                          │    - Captures correlations that a grid of shared gates misses                             │
│                          │    - Minimal parameter overhead (+1 parameter → 8 total distinct params, 10 circuit       │
│                          │ params)                                                                                   │
│                          │    - Breaks symmetry subtly without exploding complexity                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This ring loop will be inserted after the existing ZZ layer, allowing the circuit to      │
│                          │ capture finer correlations that distinguish hard samples. The extra parameter cost is     │
│                          │ justified by the worst_group_margin improvement trajectory from prior runs.               │
