│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_zz_diag_parameters                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.43) has a moderate combined score with concerning metrics:   │
│                          │ - Validation margin: 0.42 (compared to 0.58 in the second prior program)                  │
│                          │ - Worst group margin: 0.25 (compared to 0.31 in the second prior program)                 │
│                          │ - Large generalization gap: 0.22 (compared to 0.10 in the second prior program)           │
│                          │ - Lower test accuracy: 0.78 (compared to 0.90 in the second prior program)                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current ANSATZ_SPEC has only 9 distinct parameters across 22 gate operations, which   │
│                          │ is highly aggressive parameter sharing. While parameter economy is important, the current │
│                          │ design may be under-parameterized and unable to express the complexity needed to separate │
│                          │ hard validation samples.                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Looking at the second prior program (score 0.54), it had:                                 │
│                          │ - 12 distinct parameters with careful allocation                                          │
│                          │ - Dedicated parameters for cross-layer entanglement (yy_12, yy_34, yy_56)                 │
│                          │ - Separate per-pair XX entanglement control (xx_01, xx_23, xx_45, xx_67)                  │
│                          │ - Worst group margin of 0.31 (higher than current 0.25)                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation to split the shared `zz_diag` parameter into two distinct keys—`zz_03` │
│                          │ for wires [0,3] and `zz_47` for wires [4,7]—adds only one extra distinct parameter        │
│                          │ (bringing the block from 9 to 10 distinct params, and total from 11 to 12) while          │
│                          │ providing finer control over diagonal coupling. This should:                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Improve margin separation on difficult samples through more nuanced entanglement       │
│                          │ control                                                                                   │
│                          │ 2. Maintain parameter economy (only +1 distinct param)                                    │
│                          │ 3. Enable the circuit to learn differentiated couplings for different diagonal pairs      │
│                          │ 4. Match the parameter count (12 total) of the higher-performing second prior program     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a conservative, targeted improvement that increases expressiveness while          │
│                          │ preserving the efficiency principle.                                                      │
