│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_zz_diag                                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (Gen 10) scores 0.46 with 7 distinct parameters and shows weaker      │
│                          │ worst-group margin (0.25) and validation margin (0.43) compared to Gen 9 (score 0.54,     │
│                          │ worst-group margin 0.31, validation margin 0.58). The key issue is insufficient parameter │
│                          │ count and entanglement diversity.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior Gen 9 program achieved score 0.54 with 12 distinct parameters using             │
│                          │ fine-grained control over diagonal ZZ couplings: `"zz_03"` and `"zz_47"` on separate      │
│                          │ diagonals. The current Gen 10 collapsed this to one shared `"diag"` parameter on only     │
│                          │ [0,4] and [2,6], losing expressive power.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation: split the shared `"diag"` ZZ parameter into two independent           │
│                          │ parameters—`"zz_04"` for wires [0,4] and `"zz_26"` for wires [2,6]—boosting the distinct  │
│                          │ parameter count from 7 to 9. This minimal 2-parameter increase restores finer control     │
│                          │ over long-range entanglement while maintaining shallow depth and preserving the proven    │
│                          │ near-neighbor + cross-layer + diagonal architecture. The tighter coupling between the two │
│                          │ halves of the qubit space should improve worst-group margin separation and reduce the     │
│                          │ generalization gap.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Additional refinement: add one more ZZ gate on the complementary diagonal pair [1,5] with │
│                          │ parameter `"zz_15"` to achieve symmetric full diagonal coverage, bringing the total to 10 │
│                          │ distinct parameters. This maintains parameter economy while improving expressiveness and  │
│                          │ should yield validation margins closer to 0.58 and worst-group margin closer to 0.31.     │
