│ patch_name               │ simplified_ansatz_with_aggressive_sharing                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz (8 distinct parameters) can be improved by further consolidating       │
│                          │ parameter sharing while maintaining expressiveness through strategic gate placement. Key  │
│                          │ observations:                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The current worst_group_margin of 0.33 suggests the circuit is not optimally tuned for │
│                          │ the hardest samples                                                                       │
│                          │ 2. The circuit has relatively high depth (27) and gate count (90), indicating potential   │
│                          │ for simplification                                                                        │
│                          │ 3. More aggressive parameter sharing has been proven beneficial (prior programs show      │
│                          │ 2-param alternating schemes working well)                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Reduce to 6 distinct parameters using more aggressive sharing:                          │
│                          │   - All single-qubit rotations alternate between just 2 parameters (one for even qubits,  │
│                          │ one for odd)                                                                              │
│                          │   - All XX gates share a single parameter                                                 │
│                          │   - YY cross-layer gates share a single parameter                                         │
│                          │   - ZZ diagonal gates share a single parameter                                            │
│                          │ - Eliminate the redundant ring-loop layer (which has 4 gates on only 4 qubits sharing one │
│                          │ param)                                                                                    │
│                          │ - Replace with a single targeted long-range coupling                                      │
│                          │ - This reduces both parameter count and circuit depth, improving generalization           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The reduction in parameters (from 8 to 6) combined with simplified structure should       │
│                          │ improve:                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency (fewer params to optimize)                                         │
│                          │ - Generalization (reduced overfitting risk)                                               │
│                          │ - Worst-group margin (simpler circuits often have more robust margins)                    │
