│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the regression from 0.56 to 0.40:                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current design has critical flaws:                                                    │
│                          │ 1. **RZ parameter over-sharing**: All 8 qubits share a single "rz_final" parameter. This  │
│                          │ is drastically under-expressive compared to the prior design (which used even/odd parity: │
│                          │ 2 params for RZ).                                                                         │
│                          │ 2. **Missing YY/ZZ gates**: Prior successful designs (0.56 score) used YY and ZZ gates    │
│                          │ for better entanglement diversity. Current design only uses XX.                           │
│                          │ 3. **Worse worst-group margin (0.16 vs 0.31)**: Insufficient expressiveness fails on hard │
│                          │ samples.                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Solution**: Restore the successful pattern from the 0.56 baseline:                      │
│                          │ - Use even/odd RZ parity sharing (2 params) instead of global sharing (1 param)           │
│                          │ - Add YY and ZZ entanglers on strategic qubit pairs for diverse entanglement              │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count manageable while increasing expressiveness                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases N_PARAMS_PER_BLOCK from 6 to 10 (still reasonable) but dramatically        │
│                          │ improves separation on hard samples through better circuit expressiveness and inductive   │
│                          │ bias.                                                                                     │
