│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.46) is significantly underperforming compared to the second  │
│                          │ prior program (score 0.60). The key issue is that the current ansatz has too much         │
│                          │ entanglement complexity without proper regularization, leading to:                        │
│                          │ - Higher generalization gap (0.18 vs 0.04)                                                │
│                          │ - Worse worst_group_margin (0.25 vs 0.32)                                                 │
│                          │ - Lower validation_margin (0.43 vs 0.64)                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests implementing per-repeat entangler pattern shifts. Since we    │
│                          │ can only edit within EVOLVE-BLOCK, we will:                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Simplify the ANSATZ_SPEC to match the cleaner structure from the second program (which │
│                          │ scored 0.60)                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. Use helper functions within EVOLVE-BLOCK to generate a shifted version of the          │
│                          │ entanglement pattern                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach reduces circuit complexity while introducing deterministic wire-shifting    │
│                          │ for symmetry breaking, which should:                                                      │
│                          │ - Reduce parameter redundancy                                                             │
│                          │ - Improve generalization by avoiding overfitting                                          │
│                          │ - Tighten margins on hard samples                                                         │
