                         Patch Metadata - Gen 41/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_odd_qubit_yy_loop                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score: 0.46) has regressed from the previous generation (score:      │
│                          │ 0.60, n_params: 9), which achieved better generalization with a lean, well-balanced       │
│                          │ entanglement structure. The current candidate has expanded to 11 total parameters (9      │
│                          │ distinct) but lost performance, particularly on worst-group margin (0.26 vs 0.32).        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation to add an odd-qubit YY loop directly addresses this: it balances       │
│                          │ entanglement across both parity sublattices. The previous high-performer had strong       │
│                          │ results with even-qubit parity sharing in RY and RZ layers. By adding complementary       │
│                          │ odd-qubit YY interactions on wires [(1,3), (3,5), (5,7), (7,1)], we create a ring loop    │
│                          │ similar to the even-qubit pattern but on the odd sublattice, improving non-local cycle    │
│                          │ diversity.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight: the even-qubit operations (indices 0,2,4,6) and odd-qubit operations     │
│                          │ (indices 1,3,5,7) should each have strong internal connectivity. Currently, the odd       │
│                          │ qubits lack a dedicated non-local cycle. This symmetric expansion (without changing the   │
│                          │ even-qubit structure) should:                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Improve separation of hard samples (worst-group margin)                                │
│                          │ 2. Maintain parameter economy by using a single shared parameter "yy_loop_odd"            │
│                          │ 3. Better generalization through balanced connectivity                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit adds exactly 4 gates with 1 new parameter, bringing the distinct param count to │
│                          │ 10, which still sits in the efficient regime (parameter_efficiency is dominated by the    │
│                          │ parameter count penalty, not the gate count).                                             │
