│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deterministic_entangler_dropout                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.51, while the best prior program (Gen 9, score 0.60)         │
│                          │ achieves superior performance by maintaining simpler, more parameter-efficient ansatzes   │
│                          │ with better generalization. The key insight from comparing the programs is:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter Economy**: The best program (score 0.60) uses only 7 distinct parameters,  │
│                          │ while the current program uses 7 but with worse worst_group_margin (0.36 vs 0.32) and     │
│                          │ test accuracy (0.85 vs 0.96).                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Structural Simplicity**: The current program has dense all-to-all entanglement with  │
│                          │ many two-qubit gates (96 gate count), causing overfitting and poor worst-group            │
│                          │ separation. The best program achieves this with fewer gates and better structure.         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **The Recommendation**: Implement deterministic entangler "dropout" to cycle through   │
│                          │ which two-qubit gates execute per block repetition. This creates structural perturbations │
│                          │ that improve robustness without adding parameters.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Identify all parametric two-qubit gates in the ansatz                                   │
│                          │ - On each block repetition, skip one gate in a cyclic pattern (block_index %              │
│                          │ number_of_2qubit_gates)                                                                   │
│                          │ - This mimics regularization while keeping parameter count fixed                          │
│                          │ - Improves worst-group margins by preventing the circuit from over-specializing to the    │
│                          │ training set                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new ansatz will:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Use fewer total two-qubit gates (remove overly dense coupling)                         │
│                          │ 2. Implement dropout in apply_ansatz_block to cycle through which gates to skip           │
│                          │ 3. Maintain simpler parameter sharing (binary even/odd patterns)                          │
│                          │ 4. Focus on nearest-neighbor and essential cross-layer entanglement                       │
│                          │ 5. Avoid the full all-to-all coupling that causes poor generalization                     │
