│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_zz_diagonal_params                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current program shows degraded performance (0.46 score) compared to the second prior  │
│                          │ program (0.60 score), which achieved better worst-group margin (0.32 vs 0.23) and         │
│                          │ validation margin (0.64 vs 0.41).                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of the current ANSATZ_SPEC reveals the issue: the long-range ZZ coupling uses    │
│                          │ three gates `[0,4]`, `[2,6]`, and `[1,5]` all sharing a single parameter `"zz_diag"`.     │
│                          │ This aggressive parameter sharing on diverse qubit pairs may over-constrain the optimizer │
│                          │ and prevent fine-grained control over the different diagonal couplings.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The second prior program achieved superior performance with a more refined entanglement   │
│                          │ layer structure. Looking at its pattern, it used separate parameters for distinct         │
│                          │ coupling types (e.g., `"yy_diag"` for cross-layer YY coupling on specific pairs,          │
│                          │ `"xx_near"` for nearest-neighbor XX).                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to split the long-range ZZ coupling into two distinct parameters:   │
│                          │ - `"zz_03"` for the `[0,3]` and `[4,7]` pair (which follows the diagonal parity pattern   │
│                          │ used in prior good solutions)                                                             │
│                          │ - `"zz_46"` for the `[2,6]` pair (or keep one shared pair separate)                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This minimal +1 parameter change (from 7 to 8 distinct params per block) gives the        │
│                          │ optimizer finer control over each diagonal coupling link, improving the worst-group       │
│                          │ margin and overall separation while maintaining parameter economy. The structure aligns   │
│                          │ with the parity-sharing principle used elsewhere in the circuit and preserves entangler   │
│                          │ diversity.                                                                                │
