│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ split_zz_diag_params                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.46, which is lower than the prior best of 0.60. The main     │
│                          │ issues appear to be:                                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Too many parameters (11 total, 9 distinct) — parameter economy is critical             │
│                          │ 2. Lower validation margin (0.51 vs 0.64) and worst_group_margin (0.26 vs 0.32)           │
│                          │ 3. Higher generalization gap (0.15 vs 0.04)                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation in the task description suggests splitting the shared ZZ parameter on  │
│                          │ wires [0,3] and [4,7] into two distinct keys. This minimal +1 parameter tweak (10         │
│                          │ distinct params total, same as prior best) should:                                        │
│                          │ - Give the optimizer finer control over each long-range diagonal link                     │
│                          │ - Preserve the parity-sharing and entangler diversity elsewhere                           │
│                          │ - Improve hard-sample separation (worst_group_margin) by enabling per-link ZZ tuning      │
│                          │ - Maintain computational efficiency while reducing overfitting via parameter              │
│                          │ specialization                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This change directly addresses the worst_group_margin deficit and aligns with the prior   │
│                          │ high-performing variant (n_distinct_params=7 → +1 for ZZ split = 8, but current is 9, so  │
│                          │ we net reduce complexity by being more selective).                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Actually, reviewing more carefully: the prior best had 7 distinct params. The current has │
│                          │ 9. We should follow the recommendation to split ZZ_diag into two parameters, which will   │
│                          │ give us 10 distinct params total (still fewer than current 9+1=10 if we add one more).    │
│                          │ Let me recalculate: current has `ry_even, ry_odd, xx_near, rz_even, rz_odd, yy_cross_a,   │
│                          │ crz_cross, xx_far, zz_diag`. If we split `zz_diag` into `zz_03` and `zz_47`, we get 10    │
│                          │ unique parameter names.                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a targeted fix: remove the shared `zz_diag` parameter and replace it with two     │
│                          │ split parameters `zz_03` and `zz_47`, improving separator expressivity on the two         │
│                          │ critical diagonal coupling links.                                                         │
