│ patch_name               │ hybrid_minimal_ansatz                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of both prior implementations:                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From Inspiration Program (Score 0.60)**: The parameter-efficient modular layer       │
│                          │ construction using helper functions (`_build_rotation_layer()`,                           │
│                          │ `_build_entanglement_layer()`, `_build_phase_layer()`). This achieved superior            │
│                          │ generalization (test accuracy 0.96 vs 0.90) with only 7 distinct parameters and minimal   │
│                          │ depth (15).                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From Current Program (Score 0.54)**: The attempt to improve robustness through       │
│                          │ per-pair entanglement parameters and additional cross-layer coupling, though this added   │
│                          │ too many parameters (12 distinct) and hurt generalization.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Key Insight**: Parameter economy is the dominant scoring factor. The inspiration     │
│                          │ program achieved 0.60 score with 7 parameters by:                                         │
│                          │    - Using aggressive parameter sharing (even/odd parity for single-qubit rotations)      │
│                          │    - Sharing entanglement parameters across similar gate types (all nearest-neighbor XX   │
│                          │ share one parameter)                                                                      │
│                          │    - Careful selection of entanglement patterns that balance expressiveness and           │
│                          │ simplicity                                                                                │
│                          │    - Minimal worst-group margin (0.32) suggests good robustness despite fewer parameters  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crossover strategy:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Adopt the modular layer architecture from the inspiration program (best code            │
│                          │ organization and parameter efficiency)                                                    │
│                          │ - Keep the carefully tuned entanglement pattern: nearest-neighbor XX (shared),            │
│                          │ cross-diagonal YY (shared), long-range ZZ (shared)                                        │
│                          │ - Maintain the even/odd parameter sharing for rotation layers                             │
│                          │ - Remove the per-pair XX parameters and excessive cross-layer entanglement from the       │
│                          │ current program that degraded generalization                                              │
│                          │ - This achieves both high test accuracy and optimal parameter efficiency                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements over current (0.54):                                                │
│                          │ - Reduce distinct parameters from 12 to 7 → higher parameter_efficiency                   │
│                          │ - Reduce generalization gap from 0.10 to ~0.04                                            │
│                          │ - Improve test accuracy from 0.90 to ~0.96                                                │
│                          │ - Improve validation margin from 0.58 to ~0.64                                            │
│                          │ - Better worst-group margin handling through improved parameter sharing                   │
