│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ stratified_initialization_and_refined_entanglement                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign addresses the performance gap between the current program (score 0.46) and  │
│                          │ the better prior programs (scores 0.56–0.60) by implementing **stratified parameter       │
│                          │ initialization** and a **simplified, more effective entanglement topology**.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key structural improvements:                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Stratified Initialization**: Rotation angles (RY, RZ) are initialized uniformly in   │
│                          │ [–π, π], but entanglement gates (XX, YY, ZZ) are initialized in a narrower [–π/4, π/4]    │
│                          │ window. This prevents barren plateaus and stabilizes early training of two-qubit          │
│                          │ couplings, as evidenced by prior circuit convergence patterns.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Refined Entanglement Architecture**: The current program applies too many long-range │
│                          │ ZZ gates (3 gates sharing one parameter), leading to redundancy and poor generalization.  │
│                          │ The redesign reduces entanglement diversity while keeping it strategically placed:        │
│                          │    - Nearest-neighbor XX gates (all pairs, one shared param) for local correlation        │
│                          │ capture                                                                                   │
│                          │    - Strategic diagonal YY couplings (4 gates, one shared param) to bridge non-adjacent   │
│                          │ layers                                                                                    │
│                          │    - Two carefully chosen ZZ gates (one shared param) for long-range phase                │
│                          │ coherence—fewer gates reduce overfitting                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Improved Parameter Economy**: By eliminating redundant long-range gates and relying  │
│                          │ on layered parameter sharing (even/odd), the circuit maintains expressivity while         │
│                          │ reducing effective complexity. Fewer distinct parameters (keeping at 7) improves          │
│                          │ worst-group margin separation.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Modularized Layer Construction**: The code is reorganized into layer-building        │
│                          │ functions for clarity and maintainability, making it easy to adjust entanglement patterns │
│                          │ without breaking the interface.                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The initialization strategy directly addresses barren-plateau phenomena documented in VQE │
│                          │ and classification tasks: small-angle initialization for entanglers suppresses gradient   │
│                          │ vanishing while wide initialization for rotations preserves mode diversity. Combined with │
│                          │ the pruned entanglement topology, this should recover the 0.56–0.60 performance range.    │
