│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ narrow_entangler_initialization                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ The recommendation suggests refining parameter initialization per gate class. The key     │
│                          │ insight is that entangling gates (XX/YY/ZZ) should start with smaller couplings to avoid  │
│                          │ barren plateaus and converge more reliably, while rotation gates (RY/RZ) can use the full │
│                          │ [-π, π] range.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Evidence from prior runs shows:                                                           │
│                          │ - Second program (score 0.60) has better generalization gap (0.04 vs 0.14) and faster     │
│                          │ convergence (780 vs 360 steps), suggesting more stable learning dynamics.                 │
│                          │ - The worst_group_margin is still the limiting factor (0.32), indicating hard sample      │
│                          │ separation needs more stable early training.                                              │
│                          │ - Narrow initialization of entanglers ([–π/4, π/4]) is a well-established technique to    │
│                          │ prevent barren plateaus and improve reproducibility without changing the optimizer        │
│                          │ pipeline.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current code initializes all parameters uniformly in [-π, π]. This proposal will      │
│                          │ refactor the ansatz to use narrower entangler parameter initialization by introducing a   │
│                          │ helper function in the EVOLVE-BLOCK that marks which parameters are entanglers, allowing  │
│                          │ the training loop to apply differentiated initialization outside the block.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ However, since we can only edit within EVOLVE-BLOCK, we will restructure the ANSATZ_SPEC  │
│                          │ to group entanglers with distinct parameter names that can be identified, then document   │
│                          │ the narrower initialization expectation.                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Alternative approach: We can add additional RZ rotations on each qubit after the          │
│                          │ entanglement layers to strengthen the phase manipulation without adding new distinct      │
│                          │ parameters, improving expressiveness within the same parameter count.                     │
