╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_entanglement_ansatz                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The crossover combines the best aspects of both high-performing candidates:               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the 0.60-score program (best performer)**: The entanglement layer structure     │
│                          │ that uses selective YY and ZZ couplings (wires [1,3], [4,6] for YY; [0,3], [4,7] for ZZ), │
│                          │ which achieves superior validation accuracy (0.97) and test accuracy (0.96) with          │
│                          │ excellent generalization (gap=0.04).                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the 0.56-score program**: The additional ring-loop YY entanglement (wires       │
│                          │ [0,2], [2,4], [4,6], [6,0]) that provides extra non-local connectivity and sample         │
│                          │ separation, particularly beneficial for worst-case hardest samples (achieving             │
│                          │ worst_group_margin of 0.33).                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Hybrid strategy**: Merge the two entanglement layers while maintaining aggressive    │
│                          │ parameter sharing to keep the total distinct parameter count low (critical for parameter  │
│                          │ efficiency scoring). The best structure uses:                                             │
│                          │    - Nearest-neighbor XX (all pairs, shared)                                              │
│                          │    - Diagonal YY couplings from the 0.60 program (fewer pairs than 0.56)                  │
│                          │    - Long-range ZZ from the 0.60 program                                                  │
│                          │    - Ring-loop YY from the 0.56 program (adds robustness without explosion in gate count) │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combination should:                                                                  │
│                          │ - Maximize validation accuracy from the 0.60 architecture                                 │
│                          │ - Improve worst-group margin by adding the ring-loop structure                            │
│                          │ - Keep parameter count reasonable (7 distinct params: ry_even, ry_odd, xx_near, yy_diag,  │
│                          │ yy_loop, zz_diag, rz_even, rz_odd)                                                        │
│                          │ - Maintain faster convergence while preserving generalization                             │
