                         Patch Metadata - Gen 58/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ enhanced_entanglement_for_worst_group_margin                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current worst_group_margin_mean of 0.32 suggests that the hardest samples in each     │
│                          │ difficulty group are not being separated robustly enough. The ansatz needs stronger       │
│                          │ expressiveness in encoding correlations between distant qubits.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Currently, the entanglement layer has:                                                    │
│                          │ - 4 nearest-neighbor XX gates (all sharing one param)                                     │
│                          │ - 2 YY gates on specific diagonals (sharing one param)                                    │
│                          │ - 2 ZZ gates on specific diagonals (sharing one param)                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is too sparse for 8 qubits. By adding more long-range entanglement with additional   │
│                          │ ZZ and YY interactions across different qubit pairs, we can create richer feature         │
│                          │ correlations without significantly increasing parameter count (through parameter sharing  │
│                          │ within each gate type).                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The improvement focuses on:                                                               │
│                          │ 1. Adding more YY gates between pairs that aren't currently connected                     │
│                          │ 2. Adding more ZZ gates for long-range interactions                                       │
│                          │ 3. Keeping all gates of the same type sharing parameters for economy                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This increases expressiveness while maintaining the same parameter count (7 distinct      │
│                          │ params), improving the circuit's ability to separate the hardest samples.                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0604                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 6; deleted: 0; modified: 4;                                                        │
