                         Patch Metadata - Gen 61/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mid_circuit_parity_rotations                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ ## Analysis of Current Performance                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program scores **0.55** with:                                                 │
│                          │ - **worst_group_margin_mean: 0.31** (critical weakness)                                   │
│                          │ - **test_accuracy: 0.89** (degraded from prior 0.96)                                      │
│                          │ - **generalization_gap: 0.11** (increased from prior 0.04)                                │
│                          │ - **n_params: 10, n_distinct_params: 8** (parameter bloat from the ring-loop YY gates)    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The ring-loop YY layer (4 additional gate applications sharing only 1 parameter)          │
│                          │ introduced too much circuit depth (24 vs 15) without improving worst-group separation.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ ## Proposed Solution                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Following the recommendation and prior Gen 46/52 success patterns, insert **parity-shared │
│                          │ mid-circuit rotations** between the entanglement and phase layers. This approach:         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Boosts expressivity per parameter**: Injects 4 new tied parameters (ry_mid_even,     │
│                          │ ry_mid_odd, rz_mid_even, rz_mid_odd) with high sharing—each parameter appears exactly 4   │
│                          │ times                                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. **Improves worst-group separation**: Mid-circuit rotations break symmetry at the heart │
│                          │ of the ansatz, helping distinguish hard samples                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Maintains parameter economy**: The 4 new distinct parameters are highly shared       │
│                          │ 4. **Reduces depth impact**: A single RY+RZ layer is cheaper than 4 redundant YY gates    │
│                          │ 5. **Addresses generalization**: Tight parameter sharing historically improves held-out   │
│                          │ behavior                                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ ## Implementation                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Remove the problematic ring-loop YY gates (which have high gate count with             │
│                          │ insufficient expressivity gain)                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Add a mid-circuit parity rotation layer after entanglement, before the final RZ phase  │
│                          │ layer                                                                                     │
│                          │ 3. Keep the baseline rotation, nearest-neighbor XX, diagonal YY, and long-range ZZ—all    │
│                          │ proven working structures                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This restores the circuit to lean parameter efficiency while injecting strategic          │
│                          │ expressivity exactly where prior high-performing circuits succeeded.                      │
