│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ mid_circuit_parity_rotations                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent performance (0.60 combined score with 97%          │
│                          │ validation accuracy and 0.32 worst-group margin), but the worst-group margin metric       │
│                          │ indicates room for improvement in separating the hardest samples. The prior               │
│                          │ recommendation suggests inserting parity-shared mid-circuit rotations to boost            │
│                          │ expressivity per parameter.                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the current ansatz has a fixed structure: initial RY →            │
│                          │ entanglement → final RZ. By inserting a mid-circuit parity rotation block between the     │
│                          │ entanglement and final RZ layers, we inject additional expressive capacity (4 new         │
│                          │ distinct parameters: ry_mid_even, ry_mid_odd, rz_mid_even, rz_mid_odd) that act on the    │
│                          │ already-entangled state. This allows the circuit to refine the decision boundary          │
│                          │ specifically on the entangled manifold, which is critical for separating hard samples.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The parity-sharing strategy (even/odd qubits) keeps the parameter count modest (+4        │
│                          │ parameters from 7 to 11 distinct params, total +4 from 9 to 13 params including readout), │
│                          │ while the mid-circuit positioning leverages the existing entanglement depth. This mirrors │
│                          │ the success of prior top-performing circuits (Gen 46/52) which used similar tight-shared  │
│                          │ rotations.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The improvement targets:                                                                  │
│                          │ - **Worst-group margin**: The additional mid-layer refinement should better separate      │
│                          │ difficult samples                                                                         │
│                          │ - **Parameter efficiency**: Tight parameter sharing (only 4 new distinct params for 8     │
│                          │ qubits) maintains efficiency                                                              │
│                          │ - **Generalization**: Mid-circuit rotations on an already-entangled state tend to         │
│                          │ generalize well because they work with structured representations rather than raw input   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a conservative expansion that adds depth strategically and maintains the          │
│                          │ principle of parameter economy.                                                           │
