│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.60 with worst_group_margin_mean of     │
│                          │ 0.32, which indicates that the hardest samples are not being separated robustly enough.   │
│                          │ The recommendation from prior experiments suggests adding a global mirror-pair ZZ         │
│                          │ entangler layer.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that mirror-pair correlations (0↔7, 1↔6, 2↔5, 3↔4) can capture         │
│                          │ long-range symmetries that improve separation on difficult samples. By introducing a ZZ   │
│                          │ layer with a single shared parameter across mirror pairs, we maintain parameter economy   │
│                          │ (staying at ~9 params) while tightening worst-group margins without overfitting.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Current structure has 7 distinct parameters. Adding one shared "zz_global" parameter      │
│                          │ across 4 mirror-pair ZZ gates gives us 8 distinct parameters (9 total with readout        │
│                          │ params), which is acceptable and aligns with the recommendation that parameter economy    │
│                          │ always scores higher with no diminishing returns.                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targeted enhancement directly addresses the identified weakness:                     │
│                          │ worst_group_margin_mean is the lowest metric (0.32 vs validation_margin_mean of 0.64), so │
│                          │ improving worst-case separation should boost the combined score.                          │
