│ patch_description        │ The current program has degraded to 0.54 score (from 0.60 in the prior seed) despite      │
│                          │ adding complexity. The mid-rotation layer (_build_mid_rotation_layer) added 4 new         │
│                          │ distinct parameters (ry_mid_even, ry_mid_odd, rz_mid_even, rz_mid_odd) and increased gate │
│                          │ count from 72 to 120, yet validation accuracy dropped from 0.97 to 0.91 and               │
│                          │ worst_group_margin stayed flat at 0.30.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a classic case of over-parameterization hurting generalization in few-shot        │
│                          │ learning. The scoring rubric heavily penalizes parameter count: "fewer distinct trainable │
│                          │ parameter names ALWAYS scores higher, with no point of diminishing returns."              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy: Revert to the simpler, proven structure from the prior seed program (7 distinct │
│                          │ parameters), but keep the improved layer organization. This restores:                     │
│                          │ - Parameter economy (7 vs 11 distinct params)                                             │
│                          │ - Empirically validated architecture                                                      │
│                          │ - Better generalization on hard groups                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The reversion removes the mid-rotation block entirely and uses the minimal, parity-shared │
│                          │ rotation and entanglement pattern that achieved 0.60.                                     │
