                         Patch Metadata - Gen 65/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reduce_params_revert_to_simpler_ansatz                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the performance metrics shows:                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Current program (being improved):**                                                     │
│                          │ - Combined score: 0.54                                                                    │
│                          │ - n_params: 13 (vs 9 in prior)                                                            │
│                          │ - n_distinct_params: 11 (vs 7 in prior)                                                   │
│                          │ - validation_accuracy: 0.91 (vs 0.97 in prior)                                            │
│                          │ - worst_group_margin: 0.30 (vs 0.32 in prior)                                             │
│                          │ - generalization_gap: 0.14 (vs 0.04 in prior)                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Problem:** The addition of the mid-circuit rotation layer (_build_mid_rotation_layer)   │
│                          │ increased parameter count from 7 to 11 distinct parameters, but degraded performance      │
│                          │ significantly:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Validation accuracy dropped from 97% to 91%                                             │
│                          │ - Worst-group margin barely changed (0.32 → 0.30)                                         │
│                          │ - Generalization gap worsened from 0.04 to 0.14                                           │
│                          │ - The scoring penalty for extra parameters (-4 distinct params) outweighs any theoretical │
│                          │ expressivity gain                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Root cause:** The metric explicitly states "Parameter economy matters at every count:   │
│                          │ fewer distinct trainable parameter names ALWAYS scores higher, with no point of           │
│                          │ diminishing returns." The mid-block rotation introduced 4 new parameter keys              │
│                          │ (ry_mid_even, ry_mid_odd, rz_mid_even, rz_mid_odd) that increased complexity without      │
│                          │ improving the worst-group separation.                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Solution:** Revert to a simpler, leaner architecture that maintains parameter economy   │
│                          │ while keeping proven entanglement structure:                                              │
│                          │ 1. Remove the mid-rotation layer entirely                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Keep the initial RY, first entanglement (XX), cross-entanglement (YY), long-range      │
│                          │ (ZZ), and final RZ                                                                        │
│                          │ 3. Revert parameter naming to match the prior successful approach (ry_even/ry_odd naming  │
│                          │ without prefixes)                                                                         │
│                          │ 4. This restores the 7-parameter baseline that scored 0.60                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior program with 7 distinct parameters achieved better validation accuracy (0.97 vs │
│                          │ 0.91), better worst-group margin (0.32 vs 0.30), and lower generalization gap (0.04 vs    │
│                          │ 0.14), confirming that parameter economy is the dominant scoring factor.                  │
