│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_readout_calibration                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a combined score of 0.49, down from 0.60 in the prior        │
│                          │ baseline. The key performance gap is:                                                     │
│                          │ - worst_group_margin_mean: 0.22 (vs 0.32 in baseline)                                     │
│                          │ - validation_margin_mean: 0.43 (vs 0.64 in baseline)                                      │
│                          │ - generalization_gap_mean: 0.15 (vs 0.04 in baseline)                                     │
│                          │ - n_params: 13 (vs 9 in baseline)                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The problem is clear: the current ANSATZ has too many distinct parameters (11) relative   │
│                          │ to the baseline (7), which increases overfitting without proportional gains in            │
│                          │ worst-group margin separation. The recommendation to split readout calibration by parity  │
│                          │ offers a targeted way to improve worst-group margins without increasing circuit           │
│                          │ complexity.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Restore the ANSATZ_SPEC to the lean baseline structure with ~7 distinct params         │
│                          │ 2. The parity-specific readout calibration (4 params instead of 2) will be applied in     │
│                          │ predict_batch                                                                             │
│                          │ 3. This provides separate calibration for two subgroups based on qubit parity without     │
│                          │ circuit changes                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The parity split is principled because:                                                   │
│                          │ - It mirrors the inherent structure of the 8-qubit system (qubit indices 0,2,4,6 vs       │
│                          │ 1,3,5,7)                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Readout pairs likely exhibit different error profiles / margins based on this structure │
│                          │ - It allows the optimizer to independently tune gain/bias for the two groups              │
│                          │ - The +2 parameter cost is negligible for margin improvement                              │
