│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ revert_to_slim_parity_shared_ansatz                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program with 13 parameters and 11 distinct params achieves a score of 0.54,   │
│                          │ which is worse than the baseline with 7 distinct parameters and a score of 0.60. The      │
│                          │ added mid-rotation layer (_build_mid_rotation_layer with 8 new gates using 4 new          │
│                          │ parameters) intended to boost expressivity has backfired—it increased generalization gap  │
│                          │ (0.14 vs 0.04), reduced test accuracy (0.86 vs 0.96), and hurt worst-group margin (0.30   │
│                          │ vs 0.32).                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight from the prior programs is that **parameter economy is paramount**: fewer │
│                          │ distinct trainable parameters ALWAYS score higher with no diminishing returns. The        │
│                          │ baseline's simplicity—only 7 distinct parameters—enabled better few-shot generalization   │
│                          │ and robust separation on hard validation groups.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current mid-rotation layer adds complexity without sufficient benefit. Instead, I'll  │
│                          │ revert to the simpler, highly-parameterized-economical architecture that reuses the       │
│                          │ existing ry_even, ry_odd, rz_even, rz_odd keys without introducing new ones. This         │
│                          │ maximizes expressivity per parameter while staying lean.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The fix: Remove the separate mid-rotation layer function and instead inline parity-shared │
│                          │ mid-block rotations using ONLY the existing four rotation parameter keys (ry_even,        │
│                          │ ry_odd, rz_even, rz_odd). This keeps parameter count low, improves generalization, and    │
│                          │ recovers the robust separation that the baseline achieved.                                │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
