                         Patch Metadata - Gen 68/80 - Novelty: 2/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ reuse_parity_params_baseline                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program added 8 new parameters (ry_mid_even, ry_mid_odd, rz_mid_even,         │
│                          │ rz_mid_odd, plus renamed versions of initial/final layers), increasing the total to 11    │
│                          │ distinct params. This broke the lean baseline (7 params) and caused a 0.10-point accuracy │
│                          │ drop and 0.10-point generalization gap increase.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The solution: return to a simpler structure but strategically reuse the 4 parity-based    │
│                          │ parameter keys (ry_even, ry_odd, rz_even, rz_odd) across multiple depth layers. This      │
│                          │ achieves mid-circuit expressivity and symmetry breaking WITHOUT adding new parameters.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Keeps distinct param count at exactly 4 + 2 entanglement params = 6 (vs baseline 7,    │
│                          │ even better)                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. Allows the same rotations to be applied at different circuit depths with identical     │
│                          │ parameter values                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Maintains the proven baseline structure while adding expressivity through depth        │
│                          │ 4. Converges faster due to fewer parameters to learn                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The ansatz becomes:                                                                       │
│                          │ - RY initial rotation (ry_even, ry_odd)                                                   │
│                          │ - XX nearest-neighbor entanglement (shared param)                                         │
│                          │ - RY + RZ mid-layer reusing parity keys                                                   │
│                          │ - YY + ZZ cross/long-range entanglement (shared params)                                   │
│                          │ - RY + RZ final layer reusing parity keys again                                           │
│                          │ - RZ final phase (rz_even, rz_odd)                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This triple-uses the 4 parity keys across 3 rotation blocks, creating a deep, expressive  │
│                          │ circuit with minimal parameters.                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0426                                                                                   │
