│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ simplify_ansatz_reduce_params                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ The current program performs worse than the prior art (0.54 vs 0.60) due to:              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Parameter explosion**: 13 total params (11 distinct) vs. prior's 9 (7 distinct)      │
│                          │ 2. **Overfitting signal**: Convergence step dropped from 780→60, validation accuracy      │
│                          │ 0.97→0.91                                                                                 │
│                          │ 3. **Worse generalization**: generalization_gap increased from 0.04→0.14                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The added mid-circuit rotation layer (_build_mid_rotation_layer) with separate            │
│                          │ ry_mid_even/odd and rz_mid_even/odd parameters is the culprit. While intended to improve  │
│                          │ expressivity, it actually introduces redundancy and parameter waste.                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Solution**: Remove the mid-circuit rotation layer entirely and revert entanglement      │
│                          │ parameter names to the simpler scheme that worked. This reduces distinct params from 11   │
│                          │ to 7, matching the prior. The simpler ansatz:                                             │
│                          │ - Avoids barren plateaus from over-parameterization                                       │
│                          │ - Allows longer, more stable convergence (~780 steps vs. 60)                              │
│                          │ - Preserves the key structural patterns (parity sharing, nearest-neighbor XX, diagonal    │
│                          │ YY, long-range ZZ)                                                                        │
│                          │ - Recovers the ~96% test accuracy of the prior                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a direct simplification back to the proven baseline structure.                    │
