│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses 7 distinct parameters with symmetric entanglement                 │
│                          │ (nearest-neighbor XX, selective YY and ZZ on diagonals). To improve worst-group margin    │
│                          │ (the dominant scoring term), I will enhance the entanglement layer with:                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Additional long-range XX gates connecting qubit pairs that were previously unentangled │
│                          │ (e.g., [1,5], [2,6], [3,7])                                                               │
│                          │ 2. More diverse entanglement by adding complementary pairs with YY and ZZ                 │
│                          │ 3. Strategic parameter reuse to keep parameter economy tight while dramatically expanding │
│                          │ the entanglement graph                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This creates richer feature space from the measurements without increasing parameter      │
│                          │ count significantly, which should help the classifier separate hard samples better. The   │
│                          │ key insight: more diverse entanglement paths = more expressive correlator patterns =      │
│                          │ better worst-case margin.                                                                 │
