│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best structural elements from both prior programs to create   │
│                          │ an optimized 8-qubit classifier ansatz.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations from the analysis:                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Both prior programs achieve identical performance metrics (0.60 score) with the same 7 │
│                          │ distinct parameters and comparable accuracy/margin profiles.                              │
│                          │ 2. The first program uses helper functions (_build_rotation_layer,                        │
│                          │ _build_entanglement_layer, _build_phase_layer) which improve code maintainability and     │
│                          │ readability.                                                                              │
│                          │ 3. The second program inlines the ANSATZ_SPEC directly, which is slightly more direct but │
│                          │ less modular.                                                                             │
│                          │ 4. Both employ identical parameter sharing strategy: binary parity (even/odd) for         │
│                          │ single-qubit rotations and selective sharing for two-qubit entanglement.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The crossover strategy:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Retain the modular helper function approach from Program 1 for code clarity and         │
│                          │ maintainability                                                                           │
│                          │ - Maintain the proven 7-parameter architecture with aggressive parameter sharing for      │
│                          │ generalization                                                                            │
│                          │ - Keep the identical gate structure: RY rotation → hybrid entanglement (XX+YY+ZZ) → RZ    │
│                          │ phase layer                                                                               │
│                          │ - Ensure the exact same parameter count (9 total: 7 circuit + 2 readout calibration) for  │
│                          │ fair comparison                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The resulting architecture maintains the high worst-group margin (0.32) and balanced      │
│                          │ generalization (gap of 0.04) while preserving parameter economy. The modular structure    │
│                          │ allows for easier future evolution while keeping the performance-optimized gate           │
│                          │ connectivity.                                                                             │
