│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_antidiag_zz_couplings                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current architecture achieves good generalization (0.60 combined score) but leaves    │
│                          │ room for improvement in worst-group margin (0.32), which is the dominating factor in      │
│                          │ robust separation on hard validation samples.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Analysis:**                                                                             │
│                          │ - Current entanglement uses: 4 nearest-neighbor XX + 2 cross-layer YY + 2 long-range ZZ = │
│                          │ 8 two-qubit gates                                                                         │
│                          │ - This maintains the lean 7-parameter structure (no new parameters added)                 │
│                          │ - The long-range ZZ coupling currently only includes [0,3] and [4,7], missing             │
│                          │ anti-diagonal connectivity                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed improvement:**                                                                 │
│                          │ Add three complementary anti-diagonal ZZ couplings using the existing "diag" parameter:   │
│                          │ - [1,6]: connects qubit 1 (first odd layer) to qubit 6 (second even layer, opposite end)  │
│                          │ - [2,5]: symmetric diagonal pairing in the middle layers                                  │
│                          │ - [3,4]: bridges the central layer boundary                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This enriches global correlations and long-range entanglement symmetries without          │
│                          │ increasing parameter count or circuit depth materially. The strategy mirrors Gen 50's     │
│                          │ anti-diagonal connectivity pattern while maintaining the proven 15/72 sweet spot for      │
│                          │ depth/gate-count.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected benefit:**                                                                     │
│                          │ - Stronger worst-group margin via richer global entanglement structure                    │
│                          │ - No parameter increase (reuses "diag" parameter)                                         │
│                          │ - Improved separation of hard validation samples through complementary long-range         │
│                          │ couplings                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Maintain parameter efficiency and generalization gap                                    │
