│ patch_name               │ enhance_worst_group_margin                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current design achieves strong overall metrics (0.60 score) but has a weak point:     │
│                          │ worst_group_margin is only 0.32, which is the dominant scoring term for robustness. This  │
│                          │ indicates the classifier struggles with the hardest validation samples.                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current ansatz uses:                                                                  │
│                          │ - 2 parameters for RY rotations (ry_even, ry_odd)                                         │
│                          │ - 1 parameter for nearest-neighbor XX (xx_near)                                           │
│                          │ - 1 parameter for YY diagonals (yy_diag)                                                  │
│                          │ - 1 parameter for ZZ diagonals (zz_diag)                                                  │
│                          │ - 2 parameters for RZ rotations (rz_even, rz_odd)                                         │
│                          │ Total: 7 distinct parameters                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To improve robustness on hard samples, I'll add stronger cross-qubit entanglement and     │
│                          │ more sophisticated phase control. The key insight is:                                     │
│                          │ 1. Add additional YY and ZZ couplings on complementary qubit pairs to create denser       │
│                          │ entanglement                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. Introduce RX rotations on specific qubits to break symmetry and handle edge cases      │
│                          │ 3. Keep parameter sharing high to maintain parameter economy                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This enriches the expressivity of the ansatz for separating difficult samples while       │
│                          │ maintaining the 7-8 parameter range.                                                      │
