                         Patch Metadata - Gen 79/80 - Novelty: 2/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ parity_midblock_rotation_injection                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the performance metrics shows:                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Current state:** The current program scores 0.51 with:                                  │
│                          │ - validation_accuracy: 0.89 (down from 0.97)                                              │
│                          │ - test_accuracy: 0.85 (down from 0.96)                                                    │
│                          │ - worst_group_margin_mean: 0.36 (slightly up from 0.32)                                   │
│                          │ - generalization_gap: 0.15 (up from 0.04) — critical issue                                │
│                          │ - gate_count: 96 (up from 72) — more parameters but worse performance                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Root cause:** The current ANSATZ_SPEC has aggressive all-to-all entanglement (8 XX      │
│                          │ gates + 8 YY gates = 16 two-qubit operations), which overfits on the small training set.  │
│                          │ The dense connectivity creates too many degrees of freedom, especially with only 7        │
│                          │ distinct parameters shared across 32 gates in one block.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed fix:** Return to a proven baseline pattern (7 distinct parameters, minimal     │
│                          │ gate count) but inject a **parity-shared mid-block rotation layer** between entanglement  │
│                          │ and final phase layers. This pattern from Gen 65/68/69 provided:                          │
│                          │ - Tighter margins on worst-group samples (robust separation)                              │
│                          │ - Better generalization with fewer parameters                                             │
│                          │ - Parameter economy without sacrificing expressivity                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight: binary parity sharing (even/odd) maximizes intra-block expressivity at   │
│                          │ zero parameter overhead. By applying parity-shared RY and RZ rotations *between*          │
│                          │ entanglement blocks, we create a lightweight secondary rotation layer that helps the      │
│                          │ circuit learn non-linear feature interactions without adding parameters.                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected improvements:**                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Reduce overfitting via sparser gate structure (72 → 72 gates, same as baseline)        │
│                          │ 2. Maintain 7 distinct parameters for maximum parameter efficiency                        │
│                          │ 3. Inject additional rotation degrees of freedom without new parameters                   │
│                          │ 4. Tighten worst_group_margin by improving robustness on hard validation samples          │
│                          │ 5. Reduce generalization_gap from 0.15 to near 0.04                                       │
